@startuml commit_addition_limit
' Source evidence: .github/workflows/ci.yml:1-25 at c9d858bc8261bf07f5585f545b53495bf2226a56.
' Observed behavior: CI checked formatting and the Maven build without a commit-size gate.
' Target-only design: scripts/check-commit-additions.sh checks each non-merge commit.
' Design reason: bound reviewable commit size without charging documentation additions.
title Per-commit addition limit

actor Contributor
participant "GitHub Actions" as Actions
database "Git history" as Git
participant "Commit addition gate" as Gate
participant "Existing build gates" as Build

Contributor -> Actions: Push pull-request commits
Actions -> Git: Checkout full history
Actions -> Gate: Provide base SHA and head SHA
Gate -> Git: Resolve merge base

loop Each non-merge commit
  Gate -> Git: Read rename-aware numstat
  Gate -> Gate: Exclude documentation paths
  Gate -> Gate: Sum added lines only
  alt Added code lines exceed 2000
    Gate --> Actions: Fail with commit and file details
  else Added code lines are at most 2000
    Gate --> Actions: Report commit pass
  end
end

Actions -> Gate: Run gate regression tests
Actions -> Build: Set up JDK, format check, verify
Build --> Contributor: CI result
@enduml
